;; spec:   stdlib §2.1 rule 3 (reduced is read in a tail position of a literal fn), §6.3 (R6b)
;; expect: reject
;; error:  no implementation of Num for (Step
;; roots:  ../../lib support
;; covers: reduce reduced
;; (reduced e) is a Step. Only in a tail position of the literal fn does the macro turn it
;; into the Done that stops the reduction; here it is an operand of +, which is no tail,
;; so it stays the function `reduced` and the checker says what the value is: a (Step a),
;; which has no Num instance. (The macro does not look into operands: the form for a stop
;; in the middle of an expression is a let that names the Step, or reduce-while.)
(ns main (:use fib.core fib.seq))

(defun main () -> i64
  (reduce (fn (a x) (+ a (reduced x))) 0 [1 2]))
